## Summary
The Italian Supervisory Authority imposed a total of €11.5 million in fines on Eni Gas e Luce for multiple violations of the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR). This enforcement action was announced on January 17, 2020, and emphasizes the strict application of data privacy regulations.

## Key Points
- Two separate fines totaling €11.5 million were levied on Eni Gas e Luce.
- The fines were imposed by the Italian Supervisory Authority for GDPR violations.
- The announcement was made on January 17, 2020.
- This case involves enforcement in the energy sector, highlighting GDPR compliance.
- The violations are related to data protection and privacy regulations.


